{"name":"Clay Pebble","hex":"#bdb298","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clay","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mineral substance made up of small crystals of silica and alumina, that is ductile when moist; the material of pre-fired ceramics.","An earth material with ductile qualities."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add clay to or to spread clay onto.","To purify using clay."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clay"},{"term":"pebble","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small stone, especially one rounded by the action of water.","A particle from 4 to 64 mm in diameter, following the Wentworth scale."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pave with pebbles.","To deposit water droplets on the ice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pebble"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clay","blocks":[{"text":"Clay is a type of fine-grained natural soil material containing clay minerals. Most pure clay minerals are white or light-coloured, but natural clays show a variety of colours from impurities, such as a reddish or brownish colour from small amounts of iron oxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Boulder_clay_cliff_south_of_Withernsea_%28geograph_6054962%29.jpg/330px-Boulder_clay_cliff_south_of_Withernsea_%28geograph_6054962%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clay"},{"title":"Pebble","blocks":[{"text":"A pebble is a clast of rock with a particle size of 4–64 mm (0.16–2.52 in) based on the Udden-Wentworth scale of sedimentology. Pebbles are generally considered larger than granules and smaller than cobbles. Pebble tools are among the earliest known man-made artifacts, dating from the Palaeolithic period of human history."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Pebble_Dash_%2815366562092%29.jpg/330px-Pebble_Dash_%2815366562092%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_